I have been playing NetHack v3.09 on my IBM-PC for quite some time now.
Thanks to both the dev team and the spoiler team for such a great game
and a handbook for same. But I have run into some questions and/or
problems.

First off the problem. I sometimes accidentally hit the '!' key when at the
main prompt, usually when I'm typing to fast trying to get an inventory list
of potions or to drop a bunch of potions. This correctly gets me to DOS
(I run MS-DOS 3.3). I can then do DOS commands, no problem. But when I type
'exit' to get back to the game, the screen clears, usually some funny
character appears in the top left corner, and then it's over - game over TILT
as we say - the game does not come back. No response from the keyboard. I
even try a 'S' followed by a 'y' just in hopes that it might save my game
for me. No go. The only thing to do is Ctrl-Alt-Del or power off and reboot.
Does anyone have any sage words of advice for me here? I have no problems
with DOS shell escapes in other programs or even in the ones I write myself.
My "COMMAND.COM" is found in "C:\". Please anything - I have lost too many
good games (or at least hours of fruitful hacking when I use save copies)
on this accidental shell escape. I'll even take some way to disable the
shell escape command or re-map it to some very seldomly used key.

